    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d521">

                <pb facs="0673" n="561" sameAs="frus:frus1918/pg561"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/21924</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Mexican Ambassador</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bonillas</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. A–1799</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-04-20">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 20, 1918</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to inform your
                    excellency that the Mexican Government has knowledge of the activities of
                    various reactionary and Villista elements who are conspiring at El Paso, Texas,
                    against the Constitutional Government of Mexico and are attempting to send an
                    armed expedition to Mexican territory, thus fomenting disturbances whose effects
                    have been lately felt on both sides of the border.</p>
                <p>I enclose two clippings of March 31 last, from the newspaper <hi
                        rendition="#italic">La Republica</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d521-f1"/> which
                    is published at El Paso, Texas, in which is seen the assertion that the
                    Washington Government has officially declared that it will have absolutely
                    nothing to do with President Carranza and his administration, and by way of
                    coercion and reprisals will take no notice of other rebel movements against the
                    Executive of Mexico.</p>
                <p>In bringing the foregoing to your excellency’s knowledge I have the honor to say
                    to you that the Mexican Government will highly <pb facs="0674" n="562"
                        xml:id="pg562"/> appreciate an explicit declaration of the American
                    Government on the subject, and also an active prosecution in the United States
                    of those rebels who are the enemies of both countries.</p>
                <p>I avail [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Y. Bonillas</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
